  "Kit batch 2005+ (lane kit-batch-2005-20261121), hand-authored from the archived crops. NW front (Czaar Peterstraat) from w01-315 2025-06-19, straight on: one wall plane split by 3DBAG into window runs and loggia pavilions that match the photo exactly; groups 0 (surfaces 103-104, 0-8 m from the NE end), 1 (pavilion 20/29/39, 8-16 m), 2 (152/85, 16-26 m and 28-31 m), 3 (35, 26-28 m, the 14.5 m eaves step), 4 (pavilion 33/117, 31-38 m), 5 (95, 38-53 m), 6 (pavilion 40/69/164, 53-57 m). Colonnade = arcade ground, square heads, walk 0.55 of the ground storey.",
  "SE front (Cornelis Vermuydenstraat) from w02-135L 2024-12-04 (sharper ground) and w02-135 2025-10-01 (46 deg oblique, top washed out): groups 7 (corner loggias 3/51/92, 0-4 m from the SW end, grey stone ground), 8 (106/122/42, 4-11 m, stone ground shops), 9 (130/131/18, 11-18 m, brick ground shops), 10+11 (pavilion: 3DBAG panel 6 with surfaces 7/9 at its ends and panel 62 surface 76 in its middle, so the outer loggias sit on panel 6 bays 0 and 3 and the inner two plus the stone portal on panel 62), 12 (12, 26-41 m), 13 (pavilion 11/126/127/17 with portal, 41-49 m), 14 (143/99/19, 49-57 m). Mansard dormers on the SE window runs copy the NW rhythm (the SE crop top is washed out).",
  "W corner (group 15) from w03-288 2025-06-19: 4 bays, grey granite ground with two restaurant fronts, 3 brick storeys, 3DBAG eaves 14.4 m (the mansard and its 4 dormers are roof planes the large tier cannot dormer). SW end (group 16) from w04-135 2025-10-01: 3 bays, pale stone ground, eaves 14.6 m. NE end (Eerste Coehoornstraat) has no usable crop (w05-45 shows the neighbour) and takes otherWalls.",
  "Not modelled (kit gaps): the triangular pediments over the four loggia pavilions, roof dormers on 3DBAG roof planes (W/SW ends), round colonnade columns on their own 3.6 m pitch (the arcade cuts one square pier per window bay: 6 per 14.6 m run against 4 in the photo), red clay tile colour on the mansard storeys (renders slate grey), ornate iron loggia railings (bars), fabric awnings on the SW end."
